Paninda revision 009 — completed-sale recording and stock counts
Date: 2026-11-05 (UTC)
Branch: litmus_3
Base: d796873

REQUEST / SCOPE
Implement selling as recording only, without POS/payment transactions, plus
Stock Counts under Management. Preserve local-first behavior, current palette,
page-specific Kotlin/resources and fresh testing schemas without migrations.
Automatic sync remains last priority. No production fixtures/sample records.

IMPLEMENTED
- Sell retains searchable/filterable products. Product add buttons and Record
  Sale FAB open a recording form, not a cart or checkout. Home New Sale opens
  the same form. Users record completed item quantities, unit prices and recorder.
  Save confirmation explains stock deduction and no payment collection/verification.
- Atomic sale writes: Sales record, immutable SaleItems snapshots, negative SALE
  movements, product version/timestamp increments and queued pending changes.
  Insufficient stock, inactive/missing products, duplicate lines, invalid inputs
  and arithmetic overflow cannot leave a partial record. Stable operation IDs
  make repeated saves idempotent. New sales use NOT_RECORDED payment with no
  amount tendered. Existing imported cash metadata can still be displayed.
- Saved sales open existing details and update Home, History, Inventory and
  reports through Room observation. No payment entry, checkout, cash/change
  calculation in recording, receipt printer or payment processor added.
- Tools → Stock Counts now opens saved count history with search/date filters.
  New count captures active-product expected quantities and versions on opening.
  Physical fields start blank; blank skips a product, explicit zero means empty.
  Fields show per-product variances; a reason is required for discrepancies.
- Review/confirm commits immutable count header/item snapshots and one signed
  COUNT_ADJUSTMENT for each nonzero variance. Matching counts retain history
  without a zero movement. A count updates product versions even when matching,
  invalidating other open count baselines. Stock/version changes since opening
  reject the entire count; no silent rebase or overwrite. No staff approval roles.
- Sale/count forms retain drafts on recreation, warn before discarding, keep
  title/search fixed and isolate scroll content with IME/FAB clearance. Bottom
  navigation is hidden during entry. Details are separate Kotlin pages with
  per-page strings. Material icons and existing card colors reused.
- New domain models/drafts/results and a separate local RecordingRepository.
  Room stock_counts and stock_count_items tables preserve completed counts.
  Snapshot/import/reset/outbox include counts. Product details and movement report
  now correctly label sale and count adjustment types.
- Sheets contract adds StockCounts (Paninda) and StockCountItems (Paninda), for
  eight app-owned worksheets, A1 headers. Mapper validates references, distinct
  count products, physical quantities and exact count adjustment/variance pairs.
  Product/domain code remains independent of Google transport.
- Room/schema metadata remain version 1 with a revised fresh exported schema.
  No migrations, upgrades or legacy compatibility. Test by uninstalling and
  creating a new file/fresh app worksheets. Setup text/docs now say eight pages.

VERIFICATION
Focused results appended after checks complete. Three recording repository
checks cover atomic/idempotent sales, overselling/missing products, count zeros,
matching counts, variance notes, stale baselines, reset/import and Sheets count
validation. Existing UI smoke is extended through sale and count creation,
stock deduction, details, activity recreation and reset. Temporary render inputs
are test-only and ignored under work/recording; no maintained layout tests.

LIMITS
Completed sales are recorded at save time; backdating, editing/voiding/refunding
saved sales, payment handling and POS checkout are not included. Stock receiving,
standalone adjustments, saved unfinished drafts across process/task removal,
role-based count approval and automatic sync are not implemented. No live-device
or live-Google acceptance claim. No push or Drive upload requested in this turn.

FINAL CHECKS
- All 25 maintained focused checks passed, zero failures/errors. Three new
  recording checks cover atomic/idempotent sales, no payment metadata, shortage
  rejection, count zeros/matching counts, stale baselines and Sheets/reset/import.
- Expanded existing UI smoke passed: offline product/vendor/report flows,
  completed sale saved without payment, stock 12→10, physical count 10→9,
  variance -1, detail persistence after activity recreation and full local reset.
- The first recording-test run exposed a test setup return-type error; corrected
  the JUnit setup method to return Unit, then reran the maintained suite cleanly.
- Ignored temporary sale/count/count-detail/compact renders passed and were
  inspected. No maintained layout tests, screenshot baselines or demo records.
- assembleDebug and lintDebug passed; lint reports zero errors. Rebuilt after
  ensuring Stock Counts keeps the Tools navigation pillar selected.
- APK: app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk.
- Fresh Room version 1/eight-worksheet contract documented; no migrations added.
- No remote Git push or Drive upload requested; changes committed locally.
